---
title: PWR - power modes, nothing to wire
---
%% ON-CHIP ONLY. No pins of its own.
%% The wake-up pin is PA0, which is also the on-board B1 button - so the user
%% button doubles as the wake source with no extra wiring.
%% VBAT on this board is tied to VDD unless you cut the jumper, so the backup
%% domain does not survive a power cut out of the box.
%% Standby loses all SRAM except the backup registers.
flowchart LR
    subgraph MODES["Power modes - deepest last"]
        RUN["Run - full speed"]
        SLEEP["Sleep - core stopped, peripherals live - any enabled interrupt wakes"]
        STOP["Stop - clocks off, SRAM retained - an EXTI line wakes"]
        STBY["Standby - only backup domain alive - WKUP pin PA0 or an RTC alarm wakes"]
    end

    BKP["Backup domain - registers + RTC, held up by VBAT (tied to VDD here)"]

    RUN --> SLEEP
    SLEEP --> STOP
    STOP --> STBY
    STBY -.->|"survives"| BKP
